@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Important Supplications";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Important Islamic supplications and duas";
}

<div class="container my-5">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12">
            <h1 class="mb-4" style="color: #b90000; font-weight: 600;">Important Supplications</h1>
            <p class="mb-4">Essential duas for daily life and special occasions</p>

            <!-- Dua Kumayl -->
            <section class="dua-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-2" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Dua Kumayl</h3>
                <p class="text-muted small mb-2">Recited on Thursday nights</p>
                <p>
                    Dua Kumayl is one of the most famous supplications in Islamic literature. It was taught by
                    Imam Ali (AS) to his companion Kumayl ibn Ziyad. This profound dua is traditionally recited
                    on Thursday nights and contains beautiful expressions of divine praise and seeking forgiveness.
                </p>
                <a href="https://www.duas.org/kumayl.htm" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                    <i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i> Read Full Text
                </a>
            </section>

            <!-- Dua Tawassul -->
            <section class="dua-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-2" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Dua Tawassul</h3>
                <p class="text-muted small mb-2">Seeking intercession through the Prophet and Ahlul Bayt</p>
                <p>
                    Dua Tawassul is a supplication seeking intercession through the Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) and
                    his family, the Ahlul Bayt (AS). It is commonly recited to seek blessings and assistance
                    through their blessed names.
                </p>
                <a href="https://www.duas.org/tawassul.htm" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                    <i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i> Read Full Text
                </a>
            </section>

            <!-- Dua Nudba -->
            <section class="dua-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-2" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Dua Nudba</h3>
                <p class="text-muted small mb-2">Recited on Fridays and Eid days</p>
                <p>
                    Dua Nudba is a lamentation expressing love and longing for Imam Mahdi (AJ). It is traditionally
                    recited after Fajr prayers on Fridays and the four Eid days. This beautiful supplication
                    reminds us of our connection to the Imam of our time.
                </p>
                <a href="https://www.duas.org/nudba.htm" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                    <i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i> Read Full Text
                </a>
            </section>

            <!-- Dua Faraj -->
            <section class="dua-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-2" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Dua Faraj</h3>
                <p class="text-muted small mb-2">For the reappearance of Imam Mahdi (AJ)</p>
                <p>
                    Dua Faraj is a short yet powerful supplication for the hastening of the reappearance of
                    Imam Mahdi (AJ). It is recommended to recite this dua regularly to express our longing
                    for the establishment of justice and peace in the world.
                </p>
                <div class="p-3 mt-3" style="background-color: #f8f9fa; border-left: 3px solid #b90000;">
                    <p class="mb-0 small">
                        <strong>Transliteration:</strong><br />
                        Allahumma kun li waliyyikal Hujjatibnil Hasan, salawatuka 'alayhi wa 'ala abaih,
                        fi hadhihis sa'ah wa fi kulli sa'ah, waliyyan wa hafidhan wa qa'idan wa nasiran
                        wa dalilan wa 'aynan, hatta tuskina hul-ardha taw'an, wa tumatti'ahu fiha tawila.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <a href="https://www.duas.org/faraj.htm" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm mt-3" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                    <i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i> Read Full Text
                </a>
            </section>

            <!-- Ziyarat Ashura -->
            <section class="dua-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-2" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Ziyarat Ashura</h3>
                <p class="text-muted small mb-2">Salutation to Imam Hussain (AS)</p>
                <p>
                    Ziyarat Ashura is one of the most important salutations to Imam Hussain (AS), the grandson
                    of Prophet Muhammad (PBUH). It can be recited daily and is especially recommended during
                    the months of Muharram and Safar. This ziyarat expresses solidarity with Imam Hussain (AS)
                    and condemnation of his oppressors.
                </p>
                <a href="https://www.duas.org/ashura.htm" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                    <i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i> Read Full Text
                </a>
            </section>

            <!-- Daily Duas -->
            <section class="dua-section mb-4 p-4 bg-white border">
                <h3 class="mb-2" style="color: #b90000;"><i class="fas fa-sun"></i> Daily Duas</h3>
                <p>Essential supplications for daily life:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Morning & Evening:</strong> Ta'qibat after prayers</li>
                    <li><strong>Before Sleep:</strong> Ayatul Kursi and Surahs Falaq & Nas</li>
                    <li><strong>Before Eating:</strong> Bismillah</li>
                    <li><strong>After Eating:</strong> Alhamdulillah</li>
                    <li><strong>Entering Home:</strong> Salawat on Prophet & Ahlul Bayt</li>
                    <li><strong>Leaving Home:</strong> Bismillahi tawakkaltu alallah</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <div class="alert alert-info">
                <i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i>
                For complete texts, audio recitations, and translations of these and other supplications,
                please visit <a href="https://www.duas.org" target="_blank">www.duas.org</a>
            </div>

            <div class="text-center mt-4">
                <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index" class="btn" style="background-color: #b90000; color: white;">
                    <i class="fas fa-home"></i> Back to Home
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .dua-section {
        border-left: 4px solid #b90000 !important;
    }
</style>
